window.FWN_YOU_PROMISED_TO_BE_AN_IDLE_SON_IN_LAW_HOW_COULD_YOU_BECOME_A_LAND_IMMORTAL_CHAPTERS=(window.FWN_YOU_PROMISED_TO_BE_AN_IDLE_SON_IN_LAW_HOW_COULD_YOU_BECOME_A_LAND_IMMORTAL_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":601,"title":"Chapter 601 - 338: Only Advance, No Retreat","paragraphs":["By the time the Holy Emperor’s decree arrived in Shu State, it was already the twenty-ninth day of the ninth month.","Only one day remained until the Annual Examination.","Tomorrow, the scholars from the Prefecture City and surrounding counties and towns would all gather at the examination grounds—a large courtyard located between the Governor’s Office and the Prefectural Magistrate’s Office.","The examination would last for two days. They would enter at 5:00 AM, the exam would begin at 1:00 PM, and it would end at Noon on the second day.","Originally, Ma Shuhan, the Academic Administrator Officer of Shu State, had scheduled the Annual Examination for the twenty-eighth, but for some unspeakable reason, he had postponed it by two days. The scholars in the Prefecture City were not merely understanding or supportive of this change; they simply had no time to pay attention to it.","The reasons behind Liu Hong’s death had already spread far and wide: colluding with the enemy and betraying the country, manipulating grain prices, attempting to spread a plague, and so on. Each and every one of his crimes was posted on the notice board outside the Governor’s Office.","Listed alongside him were the crimes of those who had been taken away by the Imprisonment Department. Ye Jingxiao, the Vice Inspector General of the Inspectorate Office, had colluded with Lin’s Grain Store to frame loyal officials. Mr. Lingchuan from Guiyun Academy had secretly sold ironware to Poshisu Country on behalf of Commander-in-Chief Zhu Hao. Sun Wutong of the Sun Family had also played his part...","Except for a few individuals who were sentenced to exile, the rest, such as Ye Jingxiao and Zhu Lingchuan, were to be escorted to the Capital Prefecture to await execution after autumn.","As soon as these matters came to light, they caused an uproar throughout Shu State. The commoners cursed them incessantly. Although the soaring grain prices in the Prefecture City had not resulted in mass starvation, the people would never forget the panic of those days. This was true for everyone, whether they had managed to buy grain or not.","\"I originally thought that bastard Liu Hong was a good official, but I didn’t expect him to be so despicable behind the scenes.\"","\"To think I was actually grateful to him for opening the granaries, stabilizing grain prices, and providing disaster relief. Turns out none of that was his true intention.\"","\"Now I finally see clearly. In this Shu State, the only ones who truly treat us commoners well are the Xiao Family.\"","\"If Marquis Xiao hadn’t been unable to stand it anymore and confronted Liu Hong, the grain prices would still be sky-high. Many people would have definitely died back then.\"","\"Don’t forget, it was also Marquis Xiao who discovered the plague first and ordered the Government Office and Physicians to investigate inside and outside the Prefecture City overnight.\"","\"Marquis Xiao and the Xiao Family have protected Shu State for years. We... alas, we truly owe the old man an apology.\"","\"There’s also General Jinghong. The Commander-in-Chief who tried to flee this time was killed by her...\"","The common people on the streets held deep grudges against Liu Hong and the others, and the scholars were no exception. Most likely, the more they thought back on all the things they had done to try and save Mr. Lingchuan, the more ashamed they felt, prompting them to write articles cursing the traitors.","Sayings like \"you may know a person’s face, but not their heart\" were spread countless times. Even a few teachers at Guiyun Academy had voiced their criticisms of Zhu Lingchuan.","However, with the Annual Examination approaching, Mr. Yue Ming, Mr. Zhuo Ying, and others could only try to find ways to force the many scholars to focus. But clearly, it was of little effect.","\"Dean, just let them be.","\"The crimes Liu Gongmo committed this time are truly too massive. Even I want to curse him a few times.\"","Mr. Yue Ming naturally understood this reasoning. He sighed and said, \"Don’t you join in and add to the chaos.\"","Mr. Zhuo Ying raised an eyebrow. \"Adding to the chaos? Isn’t there enough already right now?","\"Before the Holy Emperor’s decree arrives, the Governor’s Office is completely leaderless. Yang Ye alone is already finding it more than he can handle.","\"The situation at the Inspectorate Office is slightly better, but I heard the Capital Commandery has been deeply affected.","\"Although the commoners over in Guangyuan County haven’t made many moves, those Noble Families have caused quite a few disturbances. They are mostly people in the same boat as Zhu Hao.","\"Salt, tea, water transport, carriages, and so on... the Capital Commandery is raiding one or two large clans almost every day. Some are killed, while others are exiled.\"","At this point, he pointed toward the Xiao Family with feigned mystery and said, \"I heard from people over in Guangyuan that Commander Li is making such moves because of Xiao Jinghong.\"","Mr. Yue Ming frowned slightly. \"Xiao Jinghong?\"","After thinking for a moment, his brow smoothed out. \"It must be that after she killed Zhu Hao last time, she heavily pressured the Capital Commandery.\"","Mr. Zhuo Ying smiled and nodded. \"Although that girl is a woman, she acts decisively and without hesitation. She has a bit of Xiao Fengchun’s flair.","\"On the other hand, Marquis Xiao... Dean, have you heard about the Xiao Family’s recent moves?","\"You should know a bit, seeing as you and Marquis Xiao are considered bosom friends.\"","Hearing this, Mr. Yue Ming glared at him. \"I am not familiar with him!\"","However, he had indeed heard about the Xiao Family’s recent situation. Ever since Liu Hong’s death, people from several families in the Prefecture City had flocked to visit the Xiao Family, all bringing copious amounts of gifts.","Take the Wan Family, for example. Not only did they gift the Xiao Family medicinal ingredients from their Medicine Hall, but they also brought ten thousand silver coins. The other few families did the same. It was as if the previous attacks the Xiao Family had endured from the various Noble Families of Shu State had never happened.","After a moment of silence, Mr. Yue Ming spoke. \"Liu Hong is dead, and the Jing State Liu Family behind him has also fallen. Anyone with a discerning eye can see that this was the work of the Xiao Family.","\"At this time, their visits to the Xiao Family are nothing more than an attempt to mend relations with them.\"","Mr. Zhuo Ying sneered. \"A bunch of fence-sitters. Since they weren’t implicated by Liu Hong, they will sooner or later be settled by Marquis Xiao.\" He toyed with the teacup in his hand and changed the subject. \"However, with Qingzhou not coming to the academy these past few days, I’m still a bit unaccustomed to it.\"","\"With the Annual Examination approaching, it’s normal for Qingzhou to study harder,\" Mr. Yue Ming said.","\"With Qingzhou’s knowledge, if he can’t make it into the top three of the Annual Examination, who else could?\"","\"Hard to say.\" Mr. Yue Ming thought of the Academic Administrator Officer who hadn’t been affected by Liu Hong, and said with a slight sigh, \"If Ma Shuhan doesn’t play any tricks, even if Qingzhou doesn’t make the top three, he will still rank among the best. I’m just afraid that Ma Shuhan won’t act according to common sense.\"","Mr. Zhuo Ying snorted. \"Would he dare?","\"Previously, he had Liu Hong backing him up. Now that Liu Hong is dead and the Governor’s Office is controlled by Lord Yang, how could he still be allowed to act recklessly?\""]},{"number":602,"title":"Chapter 602 - 338: Only Advance, No Retreat","paragraphs":["\"I hope so...\"","Just as Mr. Yue Ming was agonizing over how to pacify the academy students and get them to focus on preparing for the Annual Examination, the sound of footsteps came from outside the door.","Ma Guan’s figure appeared shortly after. He panted, \"De-Dean, Mr. Zhuo Ying, the Holy Emperor’s decree has arrived in Shu State.\"","\"Quick, tell us.\"","\"Eunuch Feng, the Chief Eunuch who arrived a few days ago, went to the Governor’s Office first.\" Ma Guan caught his breath, calmed down, and said, \"Lord Yang is temporarily acting as the Governor.\"","Mr. Yue Ming and Mr. Zhuo Ying exchanged a glance, visible relief washing over their faces.","\"Dean, with Elder Yang overseeing the Governor’s Office, the Annual Examination should proceed much more smoothly.\"","Mr. Yue Ming nodded slightly. \"If Ma Shuhan dares to act arbitrarily, I will naturally go and reason with him.\"","He had previously approached Yang Ye when Ma Shuhan invited him to serve as a deputy examiner; their personal relationship was decent. He then looked at Ma Guan. \"Where did Eunuch Feng go after leaving the Governor’s Office?\"","Ma Guan shook his head. \"Dean, Eunuch Feng is still at the Governor’s Office at this moment.\"","\"Oh?\"","\"Aside from Lord Yang, another person at the Governor’s Office received a reward from the Holy Emperor. It is the Golden Imperial Top Scholar, Chen Yunfan.","\"It’s said that he discovered Commander Zhu Hao’s iron trade with Poshisu Country and handed the evidence of his crimes to Inspector General Tang Zixing.","\"There’s also Lv Jiunan...\" Ma Guan said with a strange expression. \"For some unknown reason, the Holy Emperor’s decree stated that Assistant Governor Chen killed Lv Jiunan.\"","Mr. Yue Ming naturally had heard of Lv Jiunan’s name. He recalled, \"If I remember correctly, rumor has it that Lv Jiunan was killed by ’Dragon Tiger’ Liu Wu.\" He looked at Mr. Zhuo Ying. \"Is that right?\"","Mr. Zhuo Ying nodded and pondered for a moment. \"Could it be that Chen Yunfan is actually the famous Liu Wu of Shu State?\"","\"Him?\"","\"It is somewhat possible...\"","What absolute nonsense!","Chen Yunfan, currently at the Governor’s Office, truly couldn’t clear his name even if he had a hundred mouths.","Previously, he only thought that claiming credit with Lv Jiunan’s corpse would earn him Chen Yi’s mockery, but he had forgotten another crucial detail.","\"Dragon Tiger\" Liu Wu was hidden too deeply!","Now, not only did outsiders suspect he was Liu Wu, but even people inside the Governor’s Office shared the same thought. Li Huai’gu was one of them.","After Feng Erbao and the others left the Governor’s Office to head to the Xiao Family, Li Huai’gu came knocking. He looked Chen Yunfan up and down, cupped his fists, and said, \"Pardon my disrespect. I never expected Lord Assistant Governor to possess such profound Martial Arts.\"","Chen Yunfan rolled his eyes and tossed aside the imperial decree in his hand. \"Get lost, get lost... Stop bringing up things I don’t want to hear.","\"Anyone with eyes can see that this Assistant Governor couldn’t possibly be that ’Dragon Tiger’. Only idiots would think otherwise.\"","Li Huai’gu smiled and asked, \"Then why did the imperial decree state that you killed Lv Jiunan?\"","\"I...\" Chen Yunfan leaned back in his chair, waving his hand weakly. \"Forget it, forget it. Just treat me as that dog-fart Liu Wu.\"","He couldn’t exactly admit that he had merely picked up Lv Jiunan’s corpse. Saying that wouldn’t just strip him of all dignity; even the Holy Emperor would have to punish him for the crime of deceiving the sovereign.","Seeing this, Li Huai’gu sat down opposite him. He could mostly tell that there was a hidden story behind all this. After thinking for a moment, a hint of confusion appeared on his face. \"Logically speaking, since Brother Yunfan achieved such a great merit, the reward should have been much larger.\"","\"Larger?\" Chen Yunfan said grumpily. \"Brother Huai’gu, do you want the Holy Emperor to confer me the title of Right Minister of the Governor’s Office right now? Or take over Zhu Hao’s vacancy?\"","Despite his words, he was also somewhat puzzled.","Previously, when Chen Yi handed Zhu Hao’s criminal evidence to him on behalf of the White Tiger Guard, he thought that merit would allow him to take another step forward. Even if he didn’t skip a grade to reach the Junior Third Grade, he should have at least reached the Senior Fourth Grade.","But the truth was, he only received a few words of praise from the Holy Emperor, along with some gold, silver, and jewels.","After chatting for a few more sentences, Li Huai’gu got up and left.","Chen Yunfan sat quietly in his chair, looking out the window at the bright sun with a complex expression on his face. \"Now I don’t even know how Brother Yi is going to mock me...\"","Damn it, this was all Lin Zhong’s fault for being a busybody.","...","The Xiao Family.","Inside Spring Lotus Garden.","Chen Yi had naturally heard about the events at the Governor’s Office, as well as the fact that Chen Yunfan took credit for Lv Jiunan’s corpse. He figured it must have been the doing of Lin Zhong, the Chen Family’s Guard Commander.","This was fine, too. Lv Jiunan’s corpse keeping space here was bound to turn into dirt anyway; he might as well use it to give Chen Yunfan some achievements.","Moreover, there was an unexpected bonus—the people of Shu State deducing that Chen Yunfan was \"Dragon Tiger\" Liu Wu fit perfectly with Chen Yi’s wishes. Previously, he had used his illness from the plague poison to completely clear his own name. Now, with this incident involving Chen Yunfan, he guessed that no one would associate \"Liu Wu\" with him anymore.","Laughing it off, Chen Yi shifted his attention to the Qingjing Residence in the middle courtyard.","\"...Your merits and faults balance out, and you are fined three years of your salary. Respect this!\"","\"Xiao Yuan thanks the Holy Emperor for his grace.\"","\"Marquis Xiao, the Holy Emperor also asked me to pass a message to you.\"","\"Please speak, Eunuch Feng.\"","\"The Holy Emperor said that from now on, you can only advance and never retreat; otherwise, if chaos erupts in Shu State, you alone will be held responsible.\"","\"Please help me thank the Holy Emperor, Eunuch...\"","Hearing this, Chen Yi circulated the Black Tortoise Concealment Technique, drawing in his aura to prevent any leakage. He flipped through the ancient text in his hand, a smile curving his lips.","It was exactly as he had thought.","The current Holy Emperor didn’t reprimand the Old Master too harshly, merely fining him some salary to gloss over the matter. However, that oral decree was rather interesting.","He thought, \"The current Holy Emperor’s gaze must have been on Shu State this whole time. He is well aware of the Old Master’s recent actions.","\"Instead, the Old Master has become somewhat like a frightened bird, putting all his effort into restoring the Xiao Family’s prestige.\"","This wasn’t hard to deduce.","If the current Holy Emperor had wanted to use thunderous methods against the Xiao Family, he wouldn’t have let him and Chen Yunfan come to Shu State. He wouldn’t have done it before, and now that the Xiao Family’s situation was improving, he certainly wouldn’t do it now.","He estimated that...","The chessboard in Chen Yi’s mind shifted slightly. Several chess pieces hopped around, and as the game changed, his brows furrowed slightly.","\"Chen Yunfan has enough merit on his end, only lacking some seniority. Once the new year passes, the Capital Prefecture will issue a new decree for him,\" he analyzed. \"So... am I next?\"","Right now, the chessboard of Shu State was already gaining momentum, at least for Chen Yunfan. If Chen Yi was the Chess Master who laid out the plans, he would definitely push the board simultaneously to reach the endgame. In other words, this \"Fledgling\" had to accomplish something within the Xiao Family.","\"It seems this son-in-law will also have to make a move after the Annual Examination,\" he pondered.","Chen Yi thought about getting up to stretch his muscles. Just as he was about to tidy up the study, a shout came from outside the courtyard.","\"Brother-in-law, I’m back, brother-in-law...\"","Following closely were fits of RING RING RING sounds.","Chen Yi looked towards the sound and saw Pei Guanli bouncing and skipping her way over. Her tender white bare feet stepped on the bluestone slabs without leaving a single footprint, and the large bell on her chest bobbed up and down, swaying back and forth.","She first saw Xiaodie sweeping outside the wooden building and chuckled, \"Sister Xiaodie, where is my brother-in-law?\"","Xiaodie responded and smiled, \"The young master is in the study reading. The Annual Examination is tomorrow, don’t you...\"","Don’t you what? She couldn’t even finish her sentence.","Pei Guanli bypassed her and headed straight for the study, shouting for her brother-in-law.","Xiaodie scrambled to keep up behind her. \"Miss Pei, you, you shouldn’t disturb the young master’s reading.\"","\"It’s fine, it won’t get in the way. I’m just looking for...\" As Pei Guanli spoke, she arrived at the study. With one glance, she spotted Chen Yi standing at the desk, and a look of joy couldn’t help but appear on her face. \"Brother-in-law! I’m back!\"","Pei Guanli kicked off the ground and flew forward.","Chen Yi looked helpless. He calmly stepped sideways to dodge, grabbed her with a clever technique, and said, \"I’m not deaf, nor am I blind.\"","Pei Guanli held his hand and giggled, her eyes filled entirely with his reflection. But after laughing for a bit, she then pouted and grumbled, \"You say that, but brother-in-law promised me before that you’d pick me up once you were done with your work. In the end, I waited a long time and didn’t see you come.\"","Chen Yi signaled for Xiaodie to prepare lunch while casting a sidelong glance at Pei Guanli. \"How come I heard that you were in closed-door Cultivation?\"","Pei Guanli rolled her eyes twice, her lips curling up naturally. She pulled him and stammered, \"It’s all Third Granduncle’s fault. He insisted on teaching me some Witchcraft and Gu Skill, hehe...\"","Seeing Xiaodie walk far away, Chen Yi brushed Pei Guanli aside, sat down on a chair, and asked with a smile, \"Did your brother and the others go back?\"","Pei Guanli leaned against his side, tilted her face up to look at him, and nodded. \"Ah Ma sent a letter telling them to return.\"","\"So urgently? Did something happen with the Mountain Race?\"","\"Not in the tribe. Brother said that the Wu Mountain Mutual Market is about to be completed, so Ah Ma asked him to go back and prepare mountain goods.\"","Chen Yi realized. Before Xiao Jinghong left, she had mentioned the matter of the Mutual Market; now, it was finally nearing completion. This could be considered one of the few pieces of good news for the Xiao Family recently.","Pei Guanli didn’t think about all that. She chirped continuously, chattering about the things she had heard during her closed-door Cultivation.","\"Brother-in-law, did you know that something major is about to happen in the Jianghu?\""]}]);
